        {
          "source_id": "202.txt:c31",
          "exact_span": "The evidence before the Tribunal was that the diagnosis of Dr Epstein was that the veteran was a 'chronic alcoholic'. Dr Epstein's criteria for an alcoholic was 'a person whose drinking interfered with their health, with the family life and their working capacity'. Dr Epstein's evidence was that there was 'certainly no doubt that [the alcohol habit] interfered with his family life'. That view was consistent with the respondent's own evidence to the Tribunal that there was disharmony in the marriage because of the veteran's alcohol consumption."
        },
        {
          "source_id": "202.txt:c30",
          "exact_span": "In those circumstances any alcohol residue at the time of the collision would have been so minuscule to safely permit a finding that at the time of the collision the deceased was not under the influence of alcohol."
        }
      ]
    }
